    historyContent: {
      origins: "Tripoli (also known as Three in One) is a modern North American adaptation of the ancient European game Poch (Pochspiel), which has been played in Germany for at least 500 years. Poch is documented in 15th-century sources; Thierry Depaulis's article in The Playing-Card details its early history. Tripoli retains Poch's three-phase structure (pay cards, betting, Stops) but uses a standard 52-card deck and fixed heart-suit layout; it is sold in North America as Tripoley, Rummoli, Michigan Rummy, and Royal Rummy, and in Australia as Calliente.",
